# Spot lights (ABI 1.20) at midnight, fog off. Along the back, three spot
# lights point straight down onto the floor: a warm one with a hard edge
# (inner = outer = 20 degrees), a white one with a soft edge (inner 10,
# outer 35) and a narrow green one (5 to 12). In front, a blue spot light
# tilted down towards the camera casts shadows (from the cube shadow maps
# point lights use) past a level, two-sided alpha-cutout card: light falls
# through the holes between its blobs, so the blobs alone throw round
# shadows into the pool, and the blobs are lit on the side facing the lamp. A cube beside
# the card shadows a wedge of the pool. A dim point light at the left keeps
# working beside them.
size 480 270
camera 0 11 15  0 0 0  55 0.3 200
lighting sun 0.0 35  4 2048 60 0.6 0
clear 0.02 0.02 0.04 1
item cube 0 -0.5 0  40 1 40  0.8 0.8 0.8
item cube 0 2 -7  30 4 0.5  0.7 0.7 0.7
light spot -6 4 -4  8  0 -1 0  1.0 0.7 0.4  4  20 20
light spot 0 4 -4  8  0 -1 0  1.0 1.0 1.0  4  10 35
light spot 6 4 -4  8  0 -1 0  0.4 1.0 0.4  4  5 12
light spot 0 4.5 -1  14  0 -1 1.6  0.5 0.65 1.0  5  25 40 shadow
light point -10 1.5 4  7  0.8 0.3 0.6  2
item cube 3 0.6 2.2  1.2 1.2 1.2  0.85 0.85 0.85
texture blobs discs 128 128 3 3 0.9 0.9 0.9 mipmaps
mesh 1 1 1
vertices -1.5 0 0  1.5 0 0  1.5 3 0  -1.5 3 0
uvs 0 1  1 1  1 0  0 0
triangles 0 1 2  0 2 3
mesh_texture blobs
mesh_cutoff 0.5
mesh_double_sided
mesh_transform 0 2.2 0.5  1 0 0  -90 0 0.6
